# ABOUTME: Buildroot users table: the interactive account used to SSH into the
# ABOUTME: box, since sshd's built-in PermitRootLogin default is
# ABOUTME: prohibit-password and root therefore cannot log in with a password.
#
# Fields: username uid group gid password home shell groups comment
#
# `=tupperdmx` is clear text and gets crypt-encoded by support/scripts/mkusers
# using BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_PASSWD_METHOD (sha-256 here). It is deliberately its
# own password, not BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_ROOT_PASSWD: this account is the way in,
# and root keeps its own credential. (The manual claims `=` means MD5; the
# script actually honours the configured method.)
#
# uid/gid are pinned rather than -2/auto on purpose: automatic IDs can shift
# when the package set changes, and /home/tupperdmx plus anything created over
# SSH would then silently change owner across a rebuild. 1000 is the first user
# ID and is free -- the skeleton stops at operator (37) and nobody (65534), and
# buildroot's own packages take system IDs from [100...999].
#
# This account is NOT how the app runs: S99tupperdmx still starts it as root
# (it needs the DMX/MIDI devices and writes /var/lib/tupperdmx). Use `su` for
# anything privileged once logged in.
tupperdmx 1000 tupperdmx 1000 =tupperdmx /home/tupperdmx /bin/sh - TupperDMX operator
